shboard/server.mjs`, a Function()-based inline-script syntax check via node -e, and `curl` against the running dashboard at 127.0.0.1:4570 were all rejected with 'This command requires approval/This Bash command contains multiple operations' even as single simple commands with no shell interpolation) -- consistent with FIX-002's documented note that acceptEdits gates Bash separately from Write/Edit. The ticket's verification commands (reload dashboard in a browser, select runner=codex, wait >4s across a poll cycle, confirm selection survives, repeat for a non-default claude model, confirm /api/execute sends the real selection) require an interactive browser session and a live server plus real wall-clock waiting across poll cycles -- none of which this headless, approval-gated executor can perform. Needs: a human (or an executor session with Bash/network approval granted) to (1) confirm the dashboard server is running on :4570 (restart via `node tools/roadmap-dashboard/server.mjs` if not), (2) open it in a browser, select codex as runner on an eligible pending ticket, wait through at least one 4s poll tick, and confirm the dropdown still reads codex with model-select still showing the disabled 'n/a (codex adapter)' option; (3) repeat selecting a non-default claude model (e.g. claude-opus-4-8) and confirm it survives a poll tick; (4) click Ejecutar after a poll cycle and check the resulting /api/execute request body or ledger entry's runner/model fields match the actual selection, not a reset default. Code is believed correct by manual inspection but has zero automated or live-browser verification evidence attached to this entry.\"}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1228,"cache_read_input_tokens":53617,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1228},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_availabl